<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Views.Settings.UpdatesCard"
             FontSize="{DynamicResource FontSizeBody}">
  <!-- ══ 更新 — one label, one value, and the actions under it ═══════════════════════════════
       ROUND 8, TASK 6 REPLACED THE ROW GRAMMAR. See AppearanceCard.axaml's header for the argument,
       the published citations for 5 / 7 / 11 / 3, and why every card root states the FontSize above.

       THIS TAB IS THE CLEANEST FIT THE NEW GRAMMAR HAS. 更新状态 is a label and the status sentence is
       its VALUE — a read-only value beside a label is exactly what a Windows 7 property sheet's
       two-column grid is for, and it is what the card grammar could not express: the sentence used
       to be the row's SUBTITLE under a static title, i.e. a paragraph in the place where a
       description goes. Round 5 had already had to invent that static title (AppLanguage's
       UpdateStatusTitle) because the previous build wore the dynamic sentence itself as the card's
       TITLE — "正在等待检查更新。" is not a heading. Both problems are the same problem, and a
       label-and-value row is its answer.

       THE PROGRESS BAR SITS UNDER THE VALUE, in column 1, IsVisible="False" except while
       downloading. That is why the vertical rhythm on this tab is a per-element Margin rather than
       Grid.RowSpacing: RowSpacing is charged between row definitions even when a row's only child is
       collapsed, and a collapsed child contributes no margin at all. Its Height was 4 until Round 7,
       Task 5 gave ProgressBar an Aero theme whose shape 4 DIP cannot hold — two nested 1 px frames
       (radius 3 outside, radius 2 inside) eat two rows top and bottom, leaving exactly 0 for the
       indicator between them. 15 is PUBLISHED rather than chosen: vis-layout gives a progress bar as
       "160 or 355 x 15 relative pixels". The local value is still needed even though 15 is above the
       theme's own MinHeight of 13, because column 1 stretches it and it would otherwise sit at 13.

       THE CHANNEL HELP LINE SPANS BOTH COLUMNS at the bottom, 11 below the buttons — PUBLISHED,
       "Between unrelated controls — 7 / 11". It explains the update CHANNEL (portable / Store /
       unavailable), not the status above it, which is why it is a separate block rather than a third
       line of the value. It arrived here in Round 5, when 当前版本 was deleted from this group: that
       was an information card with no control sitting in an action group, and its version line would
       have been shown a second time one card apart once 关于 joined the settings surface, so the
       version moved to AboutCard (now Dialogs/AboutWindow) and the help line moved here.

       THE PAGE'S ONLY &#xE946; WENT WITH THAT CARD, and Round 8, Task 6 removed this tab's remaining
       glyph too — the row icons are gone with the card grammar. Controls/InfoBar.axaml still ships
       both glyphs; do not re-use them here. -->
  <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto" ColumnSpacing="5"
        Margin="11">

    <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" x:Name="UpdateStatusLabel" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
    <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" x:Name="UpdateStatusText" TextWrapping="Wrap"
               VerticalAlignment="Center" />

    <ProgressBar Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" x:Name="UpdateProgress" Height="15"
                 Minimum="0" Maximum="100" IsVisible="False" Margin="0,3,0,0" />

    <!-- CheckUpdateBtn (检查更新) is a neutral, idempotent check; UpdateActionBtn (下载更新/重启更新)
         is the forward-moving action once an update is available, and used to carry TmAccentButton
         to say so. Round 7, Task 3 deleted that theme — Aero has one command button, not a neutral
         one and an accent one — so both are TmButton now. What still separates them is that
         UpdateActionBtn is IsVisible="False" until there is something to do, which was always the
         stronger of the two signals. -->
    <StackPanel Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="7"
                Margin="0,7,0,0">
      <Button x:Name="CheckUpdateBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}" Click="OnCheckUpdateClick" />
      <Button x:Name="UpdateActionBtn" Theme="{StaticResource TmButton}"
              Click="OnUpdateActionClick" IsVisible="False" />
    </StackPanel>

    <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" x:Name="UpdateHelpText"
               TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,11,0,0" />
  </Grid>
</UserControl>
